    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0641" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.48/811</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Agent and Consul General
                        at Cairo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gary</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 23, March 30. In view of banking conditions Department will continue to
                    transmit relief funds through Agency for payment to and distribution by the
                    commission authorized by British Government, you paying proceeds of drafts to
                    their agent at Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
